@startuml
!include common-style.puml

title Use Case Diagram — Phase 1 (Part 1)\nAuthentication, Patient Management, Visit Workflow

top to bottom direction

actor Admin #DBEAFE
actor Receptionist #CCFBF1
actor Doctor #DCFCE7

rectangle "4N Clinic — Authentication & Patient & Visit" {

  package "Authentication & Account" {
    usecase "UC01\nLogin" as UC01
    usecase "UC02\nManage accounts" as UC02
    usecase "UC03\nManage roles" as UC03
  }

  package "Patient Management" {
    usecase "UC04\nSearch patient record" as UC04
    usecase "UC05\nCreate / update patient" as UC05
  }

  package "Visit Workflow" {
    usecase "UC06\nCreate visit" as UC06
    usecase "UC07\nView visit list" as UC07
    usecase "UC08\nOpen examination" as UC08
  }
}

Admin --> UC01
Admin --> UC02
Admin --> UC03

Receptionist --> UC01
Receptionist --> UC04
Receptionist --> UC05
Receptionist --> UC06
Receptionist --> UC07

Doctor --> UC01
Doctor --> UC04
Doctor --> UC07
Doctor --> UC08

UC06 .> UC04 : <<include>>
UC06 .> UC07 : updates list
UC08 .> UC07 : <<include>>

note bottom of UC06
Business rules:
- BR-05: No duplicate visit per patient per day
- BR-06: Daily quota enforced by regulation
- BR-07: Queue number auto-assigned
end note

@enduml
